    "value": "gpu-bench-amd-sdc-ecc-integrity-ubu2604"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Main Goal",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Analyze GPU buffer even-index write/verify integrity via a PyTorch SDC stub"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Validation Objective",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Validates that the even-index int32 write/verify loop completes and reports the allocated GPU buffer size plus a 0-100 pass rate. RAS counter deltas come from rocm-smi. RVS is not used"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Metrics",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "#1: RAS uncorrectable counter delta (uncorrected_ecc_errors_count); #2: RAS correctable counter delta (corrected_ecc_errors_count); #3: Wall-clock time, s (test_wall_clock_completion_time_s); #4: Allocated verification buffer, GB (hbm3_coverage_gb); #5: Even-index int32 verification pass rate (even_word_store_pass_rate)"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Tools Executed",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Run an in-process PyTorch even-index int32 write/verify on cuda:0 when available, otherwise CPU. Does not run rvs or a HIP ecc_walk binary"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Execution Details and Purpose",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Run an in-process PyTorch check that writes 1 to even-index elements of a GPU or CPU int32 buffer for yaml duration and num_iterations, then emit hbm3_coverage_gb and a 0-100 even_word_store_pass_rate, to measure buffer integrity. RAS counter deltas come from rocm-smi. RVS is not used"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Methodology",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Allocate a torch.int32 buffer, write 1 to even indices and verify those cells for yaml duration and num_iterations, and emit the allocated GPU buffer size in GB plus a 0-100 pass rate. CPU fallback leaves that size blank. ECC columns are RAS counter deltas. This is not a bit-level walking-1s sweep and is not rvs -c config.yaml"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Execution Description With Parameters",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Runs a PyTorch GPU (or CPU) int32 buffer check that writes 1 to even-index elements and verifies them, then reports a 0-100 pass rate in even_word_store_pass_rate. duration: wall-clock cap (values >=10000 treated as milliseconds). num_iterations: verify loops. memory_size: allocation size in GB (clamped to at least 0.125). pattern_type, ecc_check, device_id, and seed are yaml fields and are not applied. This is not rvs. Uncorrected and corrected columns are rocm-smi RAS counter deltas, or na when the RAS table does not parse. A CPU fallback leaves hbm3_coverage_gb blank. output_format: csv"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Execution Domain",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Validation / Correctness"
  },
